NEARS-1559 QA - FOLLOW-UP OBSERVATION (regression-candidate, NOT reproduced, NOT attributed to this diff)

Observed once on emulator-5554 during artificial offline manipulation:

  1. online, zone with 3 modules: _moduleList = List(len=3), row shows 3 tiles
  2. API cut (adb reverse --remove tcp:8000; interface still up, socket refused)
  3. tapped a DIFFERENT module tile in the row -> module switched fine (PharmacyHomeScreen),
     but _moduleList went null and _moduleFetchFailed went true
     -> row correctly showed its in-band "Something went wrong" + "Retry" (this part is CORRECT,
        and is the AC's no-cache arm working as specified)
  4. API restored, tapped "Retry" -> /api/v1/module returned 200
     -> but _moduleList came back as List(len=0), _moduleFetchFailed=false, _zoneModulesSettled=true
     -> NModuleRow unmounted entirely: no tiles, no error, no retry. Header collapsed to 113.0.
  5. a subsequent ONLINE pull-to-refresh did NOT recover it - still len=0
  6. only am force-stop + relaunch restored List(len=3)

At step 4-5 LocationController showed _inZone=true, _zoneID=400.
Backend directly:  curl -H "zoneId: [400]" /api/v1/module -> 1 module
                   curl -H "zoneId: [2]"   /api/v1/module -> 4 modules
So zone 400 genuinely is a single/near-empty-module zone, and NModuleRow hiding on a
0/1-length list is CORRECT per HomeAppBar.rowVisible (>= 2).

Why this is NOT filed against NEARS-1559:
  - the diff only recomposes the header; it does not touch zone resolution or _prepareModuleList
  - the row's hide-on-<2 behaviour is the specified behaviour
  - the underlying zone flip is pre-existing overlapping-zone behaviour (an address can carry
    several zone_ids), not introduced here
  - I did NOT reproduce it, so it is not raised as a regression_bug either

Worth a look by whoever owns zone resolution: a user who hits a transient module-fetch failure can
end up parked in a zone whose module list is empty, with the switcher silently gone and no retry
affordance, until the app is restarted.
